<!-- ══════════════  SCOPE NOTE  ══════════════ -->
<div class="scope-note">
  <b>Project:</b> React + Capacitor cross-platform mobile application for the MNCH Kenya
  Mentorship &amp; Assessment Platform — serving facility mentors, county leads, and mentees
  across Kenya. Delivered as a Progressive Web App and Android APK
  (App ID: <i>com.mnch.assessments.app</i>).
</div>

<!-- ══════════════  LINE ITEMS  ══════════════ -->
<div class="sec-head">Services Rendered</div>

<table class="items" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Item</th>
      <th class="r" style="width:110pt;">Amount (KES)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>

    <!-- 1 -->
    <tr>
      <td>
        <div class="item-name">App Design, Layout &amp; Navigation</div>
        <ul class="item-notes">
          <li>Designed the overall look and feel of the app — colours, fonts, buttons, and spacing — so it feels clean and professional on any phone screen.</li>
          <li>Built the main navigation structure: a header bar at the top showing the user's active area, and a bottom menu bar for switching between sections.</li>
          <li>Each user only sees the menu tabs relevant to their role — a mentor sees different options than a mentee or a county administrator.</li>
          <li>Tapping the user's initials in the top corner opens a profile panel where they can view their details and log out.</li>
          <li>The app shows a smooth loading screen on startup and a helpful message if a user's account has not been given access to any section yet.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td class="amt">45,000.00</td>
    </tr>

    <!-- 3 -->
    <tr>
      <td>
        <div class="item-name">Mentorship Lifecycle Module</div>
        <ul class="item-notes">
          <li>The largest part of the app — covers everything a mentor needs to run an on-site mentorship programme from start to finish.</li>
          <li>Mentors create a new mentorship by following a step-by-step wizard: choose the facility, select the programme, assign a co-mentor, and set dates.</li>
          <li>Within each mentorship, mentors manage classes — start a class, add training modules, and formally close it once complete.</li>
          <li>For each module, the mentor marks attendance for each mentee (present or absent) with an option to mark everyone at once.</li>
          <li>Session notes can be added to record what was covered or any important observations during a session.</li>
          <li>Mentors can add existing staff as mentees, create new mentee accounts from the app, remove participants, and generate a self-enrolment link for mentees to join without the app.</li>
          <li>Mentees see only their own classes, their progress through each module, and upcoming sessions.</li>
          <li>A reports tab gives mentors a summary of attendance rates, modules completed, and how each mentee is progressing.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td class="amt">95,000.00</td>
    </tr>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <tr>
      <td>
        <div class="item-name">Global Trainings Module</div>
        <ul class="item-notes">
          <li>A separate section for national and county-level training events organised centrally — distinct from on-site facility mentorships.</li>
          <li>Users browse upcoming and past trainings, view full details (dates, location, objectives), and enrol themselves if eligible.</li>
          <li>Participants confirm their attendance directly through the app, keeping records up to date without paperwork.</li>
          <li>Has its own navigation and visual style, keeping it clearly separate from the mentorship area to avoid confusion.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td class="amt">20,000.00</td>
    </tr>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <tr>
      <td>
        <div class="item-name">Offline Mode &amp; Automatic Background Sync</div>
        <ul class="item-notes">
          <li>The app works fully even with no internet — mentors in remote or rural facilities can fill in data, mark attendance, and manage mentorships without any data connection or Wi-Fi.</li>
          <li>Everything the user does while offline is saved securely on their phone and sent to the server automatically the moment a connection becomes available — no action is needed from the user and nothing is ever lost.</li>
          <li>When the app opens, it loads instantly using information already stored on the phone, so users can start working immediately without waiting for the internet.</li>
          <li>If internet becomes available while a user is mid-task, the app syncs in the background without interrupting or slowing down what they are doing.</li>
          <li>All types of actions work offline — submitting forms, marking attendance, writing session notes, adding mentees, starting or ending a class, and enrolling in trainings. Each of these is queued and sent to the server in the correct order once connectivity returns.</li>
          <li>The app checks whether data on the server has changed since the last sync and only downloads what is new, keeping the process fast and not consuming unnecessary data bundles.</li>
          <li>If a record was created on the phone while offline and the server later assigns it a permanent ID, the app silently updates its local copy so there are no duplicate records or mismatches.</li>
          <li>A small badge on screen shows the user how many changes are still waiting to be synced, and a brief notification appears when new data from the server has been successfully received.</li>
          <li>On log out, all locally stored data is securely wiped from the phone, ensuring no sensitive health records remain on a shared or lost device.</li>
          <li>All data stored on the device — mentorships, classes, attendance records, user information, training schedules, and app settings — is organised into separate storage areas so the full app experience is available at all times regardless of connectivity.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td class="amt">140,000.00</td>
    </tr>

  </tbody>
</table>

